---
import DocLayout from '../layouts/DocLayout.astro';
---

<DocLayout title="PWA Patterns" description="Keld patterns for Progressive Web Apps — app shell, manifest, service worker">
  <h1>PWA Patterns</h1>
  <p>
    Keld's token system works identically in a standalone PWA app shell. Semantic tokens,
    surface overrides, and the two-layer architecture all apply without modification.
    This page covers the PWA-specific additions: safe areas, manifest, service worker, and install prompt.
  </p>

  <h2>App Shell &amp; Safe Areas</h2>
  <p>A PWA app shell follows a fixed three-layer structure:</p>
  <pre><code>[Top app bar — fixed, full-width]
[Screen content — scrollable, fills between bars]
[Bottom tab bar — fixed, full-width]</code></pre>

  <h3>Viewport</h3>
  <pre><code>&lt;meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover"&gt;</code></pre>
  <p><code>viewport-fit=cover</code> extends the app into device safe areas (notch, Dynamic Island, home indicator). Required for the safe area CSS to work.</p>

  <h3>Safe Area Tokens</h3>
  <pre><code>:root &#123;
  --safe-top:    env(safe-area-inset-top, 0px);
  --safe-bottom: env(safe-area-inset-bottom, 0px);
  --safe-left:   env(safe-area-inset-left, 0px);
  --safe-right:  env(safe-area-inset-right, 0px);

  --app-bar-height:    56px;
  --bottom-nav-height: 56px;
&#125;

.top-app-bar &#123;
  position: fixed;
  top: 0; left: 0; right: 0;
  height: calc(var(--app-bar-height) + var(--safe-top));
  padding-top: var(--safe-top);
  padding-left: max(var(--space-md), var(--safe-left));
  padding-right: max(var(--space-md), var(--safe-right));
  z-index: var(--z-sticky);
  background: var(--color-bg);
&#125;

.bottom-nav &#123;
  position: fixed;
  bottom: 0; left: 0; right: 0;
  height: calc(var(--bottom-nav-height) + var(--safe-bottom));
  padding-bottom: var(--safe-bottom);
  z-index: var(--z-sticky);
&#125;

.screen-content &#123;
  padding-top: calc(var(--app-bar-height) + var(--safe-top));
  padding-bottom: calc(var(--bottom-nav-height) + var(--safe-bottom));
  overflow-y: auto;
&#125;</code></pre>
  <p>Use <code>100dvh</code> (dynamic viewport height) not <code>100vh</code> — <code>dvh</code> accounts for browser chrome appearing and disappearing on mobile scroll.</p>

  <h2>Surface Hierarchy</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Layer</th><th>Token</th><th>Use</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>App chrome</td><td><code>--color-bg</code></td><td>Top bar, bottom nav</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Screen background</td><td><code>--color-bg</code></td><td>Base of every screen</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Card / panel</td><td><code>--color-bg-elevated</code></td><td>Content containers lifted off screen bg</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Input fills</td><td><code>--color-bg-sunken</code></td><td>Inputs, code blocks — visually recessed</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Bottom sheet</td><td><code>--color-bg</code> + border</td><td>Layered above screen content</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>PWA Manifest</h2>
  <pre><code>&#123;
  "id": "/",
  "name": "App Name",
  "short_name": "AppName",
  "description": "Short description.",
  "start_url": "/",
  "display": "standalone",
  "orientation": "natural",
  "background_color": "#F5F4F0",
  "theme_color": "#F5F4F0",
  "icons": [
    &#123; "src": "/icons/icon-192.png", "sizes": "192x192", "type": "image/png" &#125;,
    &#123; "src": "/icons/icon-512.png", "sizes": "512x512", "type": "image/png" &#125;,
    &#123; "src": "/icons/icon-512-maskable.png", "sizes": "512x512",
      "type": "image/png", "purpose": "maskable" &#125;
  ]
&#125;</code></pre>
  <ul>
    <li><code>background_color</code>: use <code>--bs2-parchment</code> (<code>#F5F4F0</code>) for the light-mode splash screen.</li>
    <li><code>id</code>: never change after first publish — changing it breaks install continuity on Chrome/Android.</li>
    <li><code>maskable</code> icon: required for Android adaptive icons. Minimum 10% padding around the logo mark.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>HTML Head</h3>
  <pre><code>&lt;link rel="manifest" href="/manifest.json"&gt;
&lt;meta name="theme-color" id="theme-color-meta" content="#F5F4F0"&gt;
&lt;meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-capable" content="yes"&gt;
&lt;meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-status-bar-style" content="black-translucent"&gt;
&lt;meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-title" content="AppName"&gt;
&lt;link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/icons/apple-touch-icon.png"&gt;</code></pre>

  <h3>Dynamic theme-color</h3>
  <p>When the app has a manual theme toggle, update <code>theme-color</code> on every switch:</p>
  <pre><code>function updateThemeColor(theme) &#123;
  document.getElementById('theme-color-meta').content =
    theme === 'dark' ? '#0D1117' : '#F5F4F0';
&#125;</code></pre>

  <h2>Service Worker &amp; Caching</h2>
  <h3>Registration</h3>
  <pre><code>if ('serviceWorker' in navigator) &#123;
  navigator.serviceWorker.register('/sw.js')
    .then((reg) =&gt; console.log('SW registered', reg.scope))
    .catch((err) =&gt; console.error('SW failed', err));
&#125;</code></pre>

  <h3>Strategy Reference</h3>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Resource</th><th>Strategy</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>App shell (HTML, CSS, JS)</td><td>Cache-first</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Fonts, icons</td><td>Cache-first</td></tr>
      <tr><td>API — user data</td><td>Network-first</td></tr>
      <tr><td>API — feeds, dashboards</td><td>Stale-while-revalidate</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Images</td><td>Cache-first with size limit</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h3>Cache-first</h3>
  <pre><code>async function cacheFirst(request) &#123;
  const cached = await caches.match(request);
  if (cached) return cached;
  const response = await fetch(request);
  const cache = await caches.open('static-v1');
  cache.put(request, response.clone());
  return response;
&#125;</code></pre>

  <h3>Network-first</h3>
  <pre><code>async function networkFirst(request) &#123;
  try &#123;
    const response = await fetch(request);
    const cache = await caches.open('dynamic-v1');
    cache.put(request, response.clone());
    return response;
  &#125; catch &#123;
    return caches.match(request);
  &#125;
&#125;</code></pre>

  <h3>Stale-while-revalidate</h3>
  <pre><code>async function staleWhileRevalidate(request) &#123;
  const cache = await caches.open('swr-v1');
  const cached = cache.match(request);
  const fresh = fetch(request).then((response) =&gt; &#123;
    cache.put(request, response.clone());
    return response;
  &#125;);
  return (await cached) ?? fresh;
&#125;</code></pre>

  <h3>Offline State UI</h3>
  <pre><code>window.addEventListener('offline', () =&gt; &#123;
  showToast(&#123; message: "You're offline", variant: 'warning' &#125;);
&#125;);
window.addEventListener('online', () =&gt; &#123;
  showToast(&#123; message: 'Back online', variant: 'success' &#125;);
&#125;);</code></pre>

  <h2>Install Prompt</h2>
  <p>Do not show a custom install prompt on first visit. Capture the event and trigger it from a user action instead:</p>
  <pre><code>let deferredPrompt;
window.addEventListener('beforeinstallprompt', (e) =&gt; &#123;
  e.preventDefault();
  deferredPrompt = e;
&#125;);

function showInstallPrompt() &#123;
  if (!deferredPrompt) return;
  deferredPrompt.prompt();
  deferredPrompt.userChoice.then(() =&gt; &#123; deferredPrompt = null; &#125;);
&#125;</code></pre>
  <p>Install prompt UI: a dismissible banner above the bottom nav, not a modal. Use <code>--color-bg-elevated</code> surface with a border. One primary action and a dismiss &times; button.</p>

  <h2>Bottom Tab Bar</h2>
  <p>The primary navigation pattern for mobile PWA. Fixed at the bottom, always visible, icon + label pairs. Maximum 5 tabs — 4 is the sweet spot.</p>
  <pre><code>&lt;nav class="bottom-nav" aria-label="Main navigation"&gt;
  &lt;a href="/home" class="tab is-active" aria-current="page"&gt;
    &lt;i class="ti ti-home-filled" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;/i&gt;
    &lt;span&gt;Home&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;/a&gt;
  &lt;a href="/explore" class="tab"&gt;
    &lt;i class="ti ti-search" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;/i&gt;
    &lt;span&gt;Explore&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/nav&gt;</code></pre>
  <pre><code>.tab &#123; color: var(--color-text-tertiary); &#125;
.tab.is-active &#123;
  color: var(--color-accent);
  font-weight: 600;
&#125;</code></pre>
  <ul>
    <li>Labels are always visible — never icon-only in bottom nav.</li>
    <li><code>aria-current="page"</code> on the active tab.</li>
    <li>Active tabs use a filled icon variant (e.g. <code>ti-home-filled</code> vs <code>ti-home</code>).</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Touch Targets</h2>
  <p>All tappable elements must meet a 44&times;44px minimum. Expand small elements with a pseudo-element:</p>
  <pre><code>.btn-sm &#123;
  position: relative;
&#125;
.btn-sm::after &#123;
  content: '';
  position: absolute;
  inset: -6px; /* expands tap area without affecting layout */
&#125;</code></pre>
  <p>iOS Safari auto-zooms inputs below 16px font-size — set <code>font-size: 16px</code> minimum on all <code>input</code>, <code>select</code>, and <code>textarea</code> elements.</p>
</DocLayout>
